1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Kamilaroi saw — an emu made
of darkness.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The Kamilaroi and Euahlayi peoples live
in northern New South Wales, Australia.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Mostly from Euahlayi Elder Ghillar
Michael Anderson and the papers he wrote
with researchers.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The dark rifts in the Milky Way are dust
clouds hundreds of light-years away.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Its head is the Coalsack, the dark patch
beside the Southern Cross.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Its long neck runs past Alpha Centauri
and Hadar. Its body and legs reach
Scorpius and Sagittarius.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
From Taiwan, its head barely clears the
horizon. Much farther north, it never
rises.

8
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Its body and legs — Scorpius to
Sagittarius — climb into view.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Someone read a whole year of seasons
there.

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Southern crosses: true, false and
diamond. Follow for a new sky every
week.

